Phase 1 is done; the slot interfaces are stable. Read CONTRACT.md, then core/contract.ts. Edit only your own folder (stations/<slot>/, chip/, themes/, fx/); core/ and ../fab-line.tsx are frozen, and requests for them go in REQUESTS.md (append-only). To add a variant, export a value of your slot's type and append it to your folder's index.ts registry (the first entry is the default): the Director lists it, `?<slot>=<id>` selects it (theme, cabinet, table, transport, board, integrator, chip, fx), the layout reflows the line from its `footprint`, and the camera's station stop frames its `frame` points. Draw in your station frame (the world shifted along x by the layout); the board and integrator draw in the board-local frame. Colors come from `Tokens` only. Read sim events with `useSimEvents(sim, fn)` and world anchors with core/line.ts helpers, never another station's constants; step callbacks read `sim.wanted`, never a captured `lab`. The integrator slot's default is the old debug probe as a placeholder: `workTime(agent, part)` sets seconds of work per seated chip, and `sim.work.job` ({ part, t, dur }) plus `part.finish` drive welds and etches. Verify with `bunx tsc --noEmit 2>&1 | grep mocks/fab-line` (empty), `bun run test`, and the harness in scratchpad/r5/tools (shot.ts; verify-phase1.sh reruns the whole phase-1 matrix). Budget: < 150 draw calls real, < 250 viral.
